# Generic (characteristic-free) generators of the divisor ideal of a point of `Symⁿ C` (definitions)

`Work.SymQuot.DivOf.charIdeal` is generated by the values `χ_b(b)`, `b ∈ Γ(C,V)`, of the
characteristic polynomials at `b`.  Proving that this is the ideal of the divisor needs, for
each point `w` of the support, a *single* `K`-section `b` separating `w` from the other lift
points and with `ord_w(b - b(w)) = 1`; over a finite `K` that existence is delicate (see
`Submission/Work/NOTES_LEAD_jacobian_divof.md` §1.1).

This file starts the replacement: the generators are the coefficients of the *generic*
characteristic polynomial

`genCharpoly C n V b = ∏_m (T - ∑_i X_i · b_i^(m)) ∈ (MvPolynomial (Fin r) Γ(Cⁿ,Vⁿ))[T]`

for families `b : Fin r → Γ(C,V)`.  Its coefficients are `S_n`-invariant
(`genCharpoly_coeff_coeff_mem`, proved downstream), so a point `φ : A → F` of the chart
evaluates them; the resulting generators of the divisor ideal are the coefficients of

`∏_m (∑_i X_i · (b_i - b_i(x_m)))`,

and the order of that element at a place `w` is `≥` the number of `m` with `x_m = w`, with
equality for a suitable family `b` (a CRT choice over any field, over the *algebraically
closed* extension where the lift lives — no avoidance lemma, no finiteness hypothesis on `K`).
-/
import Submission.Work.SymQuot.DivOf.SymChart
import Submission.Work.SymQuot.DivOf.genCharpoly_coeff_coeff_mem
import Submission.Work.SymQuot.DivOf.SecAlpha

set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency false
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.instanceSearchTypes false
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

-- Lean v4.35.0-rc3 / Mathlib 5e0c4e5 made `isDefEq` respect transparency when unifying instances; with it,
-- `ZMod.instField` and `ZMod.commRing` (and `Neg (ZMod p)` via `SubtractionMonoid`) no longer unify, which
-- breaks `ring`/`rw`/module-instance search on `ZMod p`. Restore the v4.34 behaviour for this file.


set_option autoImplicit false
set_option linter.unusedSectionVars false

open CategoryTheory Limits AlgebraicGeometry
open scoped Classical

universe u

namespace Work.SymQuot.DivOf

open Work.CurveBasics

variable {K : Type u} [Field K]

namespace ChartPt

variable {C : Work.CurveBasics.Curve K} {n : ℕ} [NeZero n] [CurveAffineCover C]
variable {F : Type u} [Field F] [Algebra K F] {p : Work.SpecLin.FPt (Sym C n) F}

/-- The generic characteristic polynomial of a family of sections, evaluated at the point `φ`:
an element of `(MvPolynomial (Fin r) F)[T]`. -/
noncomputable def genCharpolyValue (d : ChartPt C n p) {r : ℕ}
    (b : Fin r → Γ(C.left, d.V)) : Polynomial (MvPolynomial (Fin r) F) :=
  ∑ k ∈ Finset.range (n + 1), Polynomial.C
    (∑ α ∈ ((genCharpoly C n d.V b).coeff k).support,
      MvPolynomial.monomial α (d.φ ⟨_, genCharpoly_coeff_coeff_mem d.V b k α⟩)) *
    Polynomial.X ^ k

/-- **The generic Cayley–Hamilton element** `χ_{Σ X_i b_i}(Σ X_i b_i)` of the affine ring of
`C_F` over `V_F`. -/
noncomputable def genGenerator (d : ChartPt C n p) {r : ℕ} (b : Fin r → Γ(C.left, d.V)) :
    MvPolynomial (Fin r) Γ((C.baseChange F).left, C.bcOpens F d.V) :=
  Polynomial.eval₂ (MvPolynomial.map (secConst C F d.V))
    (∑ i : Fin r, MvPolynomial.C (secAlpha C F d.V (b i)) * MvPolynomial.X i)
    (d.genCharpolyValue (K := K) b)

end ChartPt

/-- **The divisor ideal of a point of `Symⁿ C`**, in its characteristic-free form: the ideal of
`Γ(C_F, bcOpens F V)` generated by all coefficients of all generic generators
`χ_{Σ X_i b_i}(Σ X_i b_i)`. -/
noncomputable def charIdealGen {C : Work.CurveBasics.Curve K} {n : ℕ} [NeZero n]
    [CurveAffineCover C] (F : Type u) [Field F] [Algebra K F]
    {p : Work.SpecLin.FPt (Sym C n) F} (d : ChartPt C n p) :
    Ideal Γ((C.baseChange F).left, C.bcOpens F d.V) :=
  Ideal.span {g | ∃ (r : ℕ) (b : Fin r → Γ(C.left, d.V)) (α : Fin r →₀ ℕ),
    g = (d.genGenerator (K := K) b).coeff α}

end Work.SymQuot.DivOf
